# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Windows git installs default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF on checkout. Without this file that produced two problems that
# looked unrelated: `poppr init` compared its generated workflow byte-for-byte
# against a CRLF copy of the same content and reported that the file "differs",
# so the setup command was no longer idempotent; and every local diff read as a
# whole-file rewrite, which swamped concept detection with lines nobody touched.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, and `eol=lf` pins what lands in the
# working tree, so a Windows contributor and a macOS one produce identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be line-ending converted.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
